  "findings": [
    "All 96 warm or changed-warm first-page opens transferred zero response bytes: 80 used one real validated HTTP 304 and 16 made no request under fresh must-revalidate.",
    "Fresh max-age without must-revalidate still caused conditional requests in the locked engine; fresh max-age with must-revalidate skipped revalidation. These are observed old-engine semantics, not an application policy recommendation.",
    "All 32 changed-resource observations fetched the new bytes with HTTP 206, and every resident cache block and rendered tested page matched the corresponding local version. Changed resources were tested after stale headers, not while a fresh cache entry remained valid.",
    "Progressive first-page opens cached 355451 bytes in 6 GETs for the original GCC PDF and 200290 bytes in 4 GETs for its linearized version. This differs from the earlier non-progressive test and does not imply UI time-to-sharp.",
    "Opening later pages after sparse first-page caching fetched missing blocks: 2883584 additional bytes for original GCC and 3211264 for linearized GCC, preserving cache and raster parity.",
    "The earlier server did not implement 304. Its re-download result cannot establish that warm cached documents always re-download when servers correctly implement conditional requests."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Four ABBA processes total; only two uninstrumented observations per exact scenario. Policies and pages are not independent process replicates.",
    "Loopback server and 384px backend rasters; no WAN or UI latency claim. Local reference PDF was preloaded in the process; OS file cache was not cleared.",
    "Late-page rendering and cache verification happen outside firstRasterUs; total request/byte counts include those later actions.",
    "No disk-cache quota, credential lifetime, physical device, or long-term eviction result is implied.",
    "No performance change to Otzaria or upgrade of its Flutter/pdfrx dependencies is included in this measurement."
  ]
}
